{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01BRwSU5QSeWaSushr9ZkYZc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//\n2\t// Created by Anfernee Jervis on 8/27/22.\n3\t//\n4\t\n5\t\n6\tvoid screen_append(const char *str, int size);\n7\t\n8\t\n9\ttypedef struct Cursor {\n10\t    int x;\n11\t    int y;\n12\t} Cursor;\n13\t\n14\t\n15\tstruct VirtualScreen {\n16\t    char* buffer;           // Contents on the screen (text & escape codes)\n17\t    int buf_pos;\n18\t    int len;\n19\t    Cursor cursor;\n20\t    int width;\n21\t    int height;\n22\t    int render_start_line;\n23\t};\n24\t\n25\t/*\n26\t * Returns the number of screen rows required to print a line of the given length.\n27\t * undefined for line_length < 0\n28\t * */\n29\tint required_screen_rows(int line_length, int screen_width) {\n30\t\n31\t    // lines required is the number of times the screen width is filled len/width + 1 if there's a remainder\n32\t    if (line_length == 0) {\n33\t        return 1;\n34\t\n35\t    } else {\n36\t        return (line_length / screen_width) + ((line_length % screen_width) > 0);\n37\t    }\n38\t}\n39\t\n40\t/*\n41\t * TODO: I can retroactively calculate this in the logic in the function that moves the cursor.\n42\t * TODO: If i want to jump to file lines, I can then just call the function that moves the cursor x times\n43\t *\n44\t * TODO: After the cursor is moved to a new line, I can calculate what position the render start line needs\n45\t * to be to keep the cursor visible. If cursor is above it, shift upwards. If below, shift downwards, ensuring enough\n46\t * space for the cursor to be visible.\n47\t *\n48\t * Determines whether the cursor is off the screen, if so, shifts the display part of the buffer until\n49\t * the cursor is back in view.\n50\t * */\n51\tvoid move_cursor_in_view(TextBuffer* buffer, struct VirtualScreen* screen){\n52\t\n53\t    Cursor buffer_cursor = {buffer->cursorRow, buffer->cursorCol};\n54\t\n55\t    int cumul_req_rows 